%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bfbabd22c62c640a6ba459d46825055b, type: 3}
  m_Name: README
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  header:
    title: Starter Pack README
    icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 83f0684dab5534e2492f651aaaf4a151, type: 3}
  sections:
  - subHeader1: Intro
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'It''s common in games to offer a one-time virtual purchase, such as a
      Starter Pack, to give players a boost with getting started with first playing
      your game or when players delete their game save and start again. '
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: This sample shows how to create a one-time deal Starter Pack in your game
      that a player can purchase with in-game currency.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: Implementation Overview
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'First, decide the price of a Starter Pack and ensure the player has enough
      in-game currency to purchase one. This sample uses gems as the in-game currency.
      To simplify a purchase for a player, this sample scene shows a button that
      grants a player 10 gems when they click it, so they have enough gems for a
      Starter Pack. '
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'When a player presses the button to buy the Starter Pack, a request is
      sent to the Cloud Code service to execute the StarterPack_PurchaseStarterPack
      function. '
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'The Cloud Code module function:'
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList:
    - body: Verifies the player has not yet claimed this one-time deal.
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: Makes the purchase.
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: Sends an update to Cloud Save directly so we know in the future that
        this player has already claimed this one-time deal.
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'After purchasing a Starter Pack, the player can''t claim another one unless
      they reset their game save. To illustrate this, this sample scene shows a button
      to reset the Starter Pack flag so the player can purchase it again. '
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: Packages Required
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: These packages were used to implement this Starter Pack sample.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList:
    - body: 'Authentication: Automatically signs in the user anonymously to keep
        track of their data on the server side.'
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: 'Cloud Code: Keeps important validation logic on the server side. '
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: 'Cloud Save: We store small pieces of special information in Cloud Save,
        such as a flag that says this user did already claim their Starter Pack,
        as well as the player''s currency balances and inventory in the player_economy
        key. '
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: 'Economy: Keeps track of the player''s currencies and inventory. '
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: 'Remote Config: Provides the economy catalog, including the Starter Pack
        Virtual Purchase definition. '
      bodyFormat: 0
      bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: See the package docs to learn how to install and configure these SDKs in
      your project.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList:
    - linkText: Authentication
      url: https://docs.unity.com/authentication/IntroUnityAuthentication.html
    - linkText: Cloud Code
      url: https://docs.unity.com/cloud-code/implementation.html
    - linkText: Cloud Save
      url: https://docs.unity.com/cloud-save/index.html#Implementation
    - linkText: Deployment
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.services.deployment@1.2
    - linkText: Remote Config
      url: https://docs.unity.com/remote-config
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: To use these services in your game, activate each service for your Organization
      and project in the Unity Dashboard.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList:
    - linkText: Unity Dashboard
      url: https://dashboard.unity3d.com/
  - subHeader1: Unity Cloud services configuration
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'To replicate this sample scene''s setup in your own Unity project, we need to configure the following items:'
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList:
    - body: The SampleGameModule Cloud Code module
    - body: Remote Config economy catalog values
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: To configure these items you can use the Deployment package, or manually enter them using the Unity Cloud Dashboard. The recommended best practice is to use the Deployment package as it greatly accelerates this process.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: Using the Deployment package
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'Here are the steps to deploy configuration using the Deployment package:'
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList:
    - body: Open the Deployment window
      linkList: 
      - linkText: Deployment window
        url: https://dashboard.unity3d.com/
    - body: Check in `Common` and `Starter Pack`
    - body: Click `Deploy Selection`
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: 
    body: 'This will deploy all the necessary items.'
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: Using the Dashboard
    subHeader3: 
    body: You can use the Unity Cloud Dashboard to manually configure your services by project and environment. Refer to the following sections to configure this sample.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    linkList:
    - linkText: Dashboard
      url: dashboard.unity3d.com
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: Remote Config Economy Catalog
    body: 'The economy catalog is stored in Remote Config and deployed from Assets/Common/Config
      as Code/economy_config.rc. The following resources are defined as entries in
      the ECONOMY_CURRENCIES, ECONOMY_ITEMS and ECONOMY_VIRTUAL_PURCHASES keys:'
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList:
    - body: Gem
      bodyFormat: 1
      bulletList:
      - body: The currency cost of the Starter Pack
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'ID: "GEM"'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: Coin
      bodyFormat: 1
      bulletList:
      - body: A currency reward from the Starter Pack
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'ID: "COIN"'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: Pearl
      bodyFormat: 1
      bulletList:
      - body: ' A currency reward from the Starter Pack'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'ID: "PEARL"'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: Sword
      bodyFormat: 1
      bulletList:
      - body: An inventory item reward from the Starter Pack
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'ID: "SWORD"'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    - body: Starter Pack
      bodyFormat: 1
      bulletList:
      - body: A Virtual Purchase required to process the Starter Pack purchase
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'ID: "STARTER_PACK_PURCHASE"'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'Cost:'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList:
        - body: 10 Gems
          bodyFormat: 0
          bulletList: []
      - body: 'Rewards:'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList:
        - body: 100 Coins
          bodyFormat: 0
          bulletList: []
        - body: 1 Sword
          bodyFormat: 0
          bulletList: []
        - body: 10 Pearls
          bodyFormat: 0
          bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    linkList: []
  - subHeader1: 
    subHeader2: 
    subHeader3: Cloud Code module functions
    body: To publish them, deploy the SampleGameModule module through Assets/Common/Config as Code/SampleGameModule.ccmr in the Deployment window.
    bodyFormat: 0
    boxCallout: 
    bulletList:
    - body: 'StarterPack_PurchaseStarterPack:'
      bodyFormat: 1
      bulletList:
      - body: 'Parameters: `none`'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      - body: 'Location: "SampleGameModule/Project/Services/StarterPackService.cs"'
        bodyFormat: 0
        bulletList: []
      linkList: []
    linkList: []

